5-04-52-350867Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Compare checkpoint `b806c425826b829eb140e9bb9677215f475ae75f` with the later failing test variant and retain the 5-test implementation that passed native verification.\n2. Clean the coordinate’s build outputs and rerun its full test task; if `TestContextManager` remains necessary, wire Spring Test AOT generation into the test setup rather than adding unrelated hand-written metadata.\n3. Regenerate the dynamic-access coverage report and metrics after native tests pass.\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791375497269}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_qJBE6Ip5VkwX3Aje7tvkNnCe|fc_0758bdf2991f2e32016ac63888e60c87d0969e56a3ccddfd3a", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No changes made. The bounded reporter context contains no requested metadata. The `AotTestContextInitializers__Generated` failure is test-infrastructure AOT behavior, not a reporter-requested entry, so adding hand-written metadata would violate the task’s scope. Tests were not run.\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791375497270}]}
